        "sha": "3b6270d5f99e2669b1b9b07390a78300236f997b",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/3b6270d5f99e2669b1b9b07390a78300236f997b"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 3b6270d5f99e2669b1b9b07390a78300236f997b\nparent d1d1409d170aa47663b6c84815176476e40d8cec\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1794086535 +0100\ncommitter Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1794224096 +0100\n\ncrypto: copy HMAC state instead of rehashing key pads\n\nEach HKDF expansion hashes the same two HMAC key pads, costing two SHA256 compressions before hashing the label.\nPrepare those states once per HKDF context and replace the repeated hashing with a copy of the prepared HMAC state.\nAcross BIP324's six expansions this saves ten SHA256 compressions, with identical derived bytes.\nCleanse the temporary extracted secret after constructing the prepared state.\n",
